course: dictionary
lesson: 5820
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Magnum is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which is its context, and try each meaning in the sentence.
explain: «A magnum of champagne» means a big bottle that holds twice as much as a normal bottle. At a party, the word is about a bottle, not a gun or an ice cream.
explain: In a detective story, a magnum is a powerful handgun. The clues would be words like police, bullets or chase. Magnum with a capital M is also a brand name for a chocolate-coated ice cream on a stick, and «a Magnum» is a common way to ask for one.
explain: In art and English lessons, «magnum opus» means a person's greatest work. When you see magnum next to opus, do not think of a bottle or a gun. Think of a great piece of work.
fact: Magnum has several meanings, so always check the context to find the right one.
fact: A magnum is a wine or champagne bottle holding 1.5 litres, which is twice as much as a normal bottle.
fact: A magnum can also be a powerful gun or bullet, as in detective stories and films.
fact: «A Magnum» is an ice cream on a stick, coated in chocolate.
fact: Magnum opus means a person's greatest work, such as an artist's best painting.
exercise: At the party, the adults opened a magnum of champagne. What is a magnum here? | A powerful handgun | *A bottle holding twice as much as a normal bottle | A chocolate-coated ice cream on a stick | A painting by a famous artist
exercise: The detective pulled out his magnum and checked the bullets. What does magnum mean here? | A brand of ice cream | A bottle of wine | A great work of art | *A powerful gun
exercise: What does magnum opus mean? | *A person's greatest work | A large bottle of champagne | A detective's gun | A type of ice cream
test: Ella asked the shop for «a Magnum» on a hot day. What is a Magnum? | A powerful gun | A wine bottle holding 1.5 litres | *An ice cream on a stick | A bottle of champagne
test: The painter's magnum opus took ten years to finish. What does magnum opus mean? | A powerful bullet | *Her greatest work | A type of chocolate | A bottle that holds twice as much
exam: The waiter carried a magnum of champagne to the table. What does magnum mean here? | A chocolate ice cream on a stick | A famous painting | *A bottle holding twice as much as a normal bottle | A powerful gun
